// The thirteen display keys and the five `hw_*` keys are read from INSIDE
// `config` only (a bounded read of that object, never a flat scan of the body,
// FC-7), each by its exact JSON kind (a quoted number is unreadable, FC-11),
// each clamped independently so one bad value never costs its neighbours. An
// unknown `lcd_layout` is compact; an unknown hardware value keeps the current
// one. `KEYS` is derived from `button_map`: every key whose meaning is not a
// `minutes:N` grant (HW-7).
//
// Every name the reader could not read goes into the drift list the next
// heartbeat reports (§11.2).
